 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Gate drive",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The threshold lies between 0.3 V and 1.0 V (0.6 V typical) at 250 µA. On-resistance is specified at two drive levels: 61 mΩ typical, 90 mΩ maximum at VGS = 4.5 V and 3.6 A; 80 mΩ typical, 120 mΩ maximum at VGS = 2.5 V and 3.1 A. The gate is rated ±12 V, leaks at most ±10 µA at ±10 V, and has 2.7 Ω of internal resistance."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Gate protection",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "A protection diode is built in between gate and source, so the gate is ESD protected."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Switching",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Charge to bring the gate to 4.5 V is 1.4 nC typical (2.8 nC to 10 V), with VDS = 10 V and 3.6 A. Into a 2.78 Ω load from 10 V, driven at 4.5 V through 1 Ω, it turns on with 0.6 ns delay and 2.7 ns rise, and off with 4.2 ns delay and 1.7 ns fall. All dynamic figures (capacitances, gate resistance, charges, switching and recovery times) are guaranteed by design and not tested in production."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Temperature",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "On-resistance rises with junction temperature: normalized to 25 °C it is about 0.75 at -50 °C and about 1.62 at 150 °C, alike for both drive levels. The threshold falls as the junction warms, from about 0.72 V at -50 °C to about 0.27 V at 150 °C at 250 µA."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Heat",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "On the smallest recommended pad the part dissipates 0.66 W with 192 °C/W junction to ambient; on 1 in² of 2 oz copper it dissipates 1.1 W with 115 °C/W. The continuous current ratings (2.8 A at 25 °C, 2.2 A at 70 °C) and the 1.1 A body-diode rating assume the 1 in² board. Junction and storage range is -55 °C to +150 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Body diode",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The source-to-drain diode drops 0.7 V typical, 1.2 V maximum at 1.0 A. Recovering from 3.6 A at 100 A/µs it takes 5.3 ns and 0.5 nC."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Pulsed operation",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Pulses of 10 µs at 1 % duty may reach 12 A. The safe operating area (Figure 12) is for single pulses with TJ(max) 150 °C, case at 25 °C and VGS = 4.5 V; Figure 13 gives the transient thermal response for duty cycles from 0.005 to 0.9."
  }
